comments.message:
@ed@tanous.net I just confirmed with our engineering team that the AST2700 A2 will continue to use a prebuilt Caliptra image.
The Caliptra image includes the Firmware Manifest, Caliptra FMC binary, and Caliptra RT binary. The Caliptra FMC and RT binaries were built from the caliptra-sw project(https://github.com/chipsalliance/caliptra-sw/commit/51ff0a89f169bbf8e06acb49b31db555e99fefb6). The Firmware Manifest includes our key hash and signature.
On MP parts, the vendor key hash is fused in OTP. Therefore, without our private key, any image built from source cannot be authenticated (the key-hash check will fail) and will not boot.
